WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:17.011
do you mean, someone dumped frogs in the pool?"

2
00:00:17.372 --> 00:00:18.132
Maggie asked.

3
00:00:19.213 --> 00:00:21.674
"I mean just what I said," Cole replied.

4
00:00:21.694 --> 00:00:26.657
"All the swimmers were helping the coach carry some stuff to the pool from his car.

5
00:00:27.997 --> 00:00:30.319
When we got to the pool, we saw the frogs.

6
00:00:30.959 --> 00:00:32.680
About twelve of them were swimming around."

7
00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:37.161
"Are you sure the frogs didn't hop into the pool by themselves?"

8
00:00:37.581 --> 00:00:38.301
Henry asked.

9
00:00:39.422 --> 00:00:40.142
Cole nodded.

10
00:00:40.162 --> 00:00:41.602
"I'm sure.

11
00:00:42.562 --> 00:00:44.623
These aren't the kind of frogs you see around here."

12
00:00:44.643 --> 00:00:49.004
"Okay. If you say so," Maggie said with a shrug.

13
00:00:49.024 --> 00:00:51.205
"You're the frog expert."

14
00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:53.665
"That's the problem!"

15
00:00:54.666 --> 00:00:56.406
Cole looked more worried than ever.

16
00:00:56.426 --> 00:00:59.927
"A few of the other swimmers know I like frogs.

17
00:01:00.988 --> 00:01:02.328
That's why they think I did it.

18
00:01:03.372 --> 00:01:05.893
But I would never throw a bunch of frogs into pool water.

19
00:01:06.914 --> 00:01:08.095
It's not healthy for them."

20
00:01:09.155 --> 00:01:09.695
"Why not?"

21
00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:10.736
Maggie asked.

22
00:01:10.756 --> 00:01:13.237
"I thought frogs liked water."

23
00:01:13.257 --> 00:01:16.099
"They do," Cole said.

24
00:01:16.119 --> 00:01:18.880
"But pool water has chlorine in it.

25
00:01:19.901 --> 00:01:21.022
That can be bad for them."

26
00:01:21.042 --> 00:01:23.203
"Did you tell everyone that?"

27
00:01:23.603 --> 00:01:24.383
Henry asked.

28
00:01:24.403 --> 00:01:28.946
"Yes, but most of them still think I did it," Cole said.

29
00:01:28.966 --> 00:01:32.788
"I need The Lemonade Detectives to help me clear my name!"

30
00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:37.520
"We're on the case!"

31
00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:38.621
said Maggie.

32
00:01:39.821 --> 00:01:42.482
Henry and Maggie closed down the lemonade stand.

33
00:01:43.762 --> 00:01:45.603
Then they walked to the pool with Cole.

34
00:01:48.024 --> 00:01:52.705
When they arrived, a bunch of kids were in the pool with nets, still chasing the frogs.

35
00:01:54.105 --> 00:01:57.587
Someone had put buckets of fresh water near the edge of the pool.

36
00:01:58.707 --> 00:02:01.928
Whenever the swimmers caught a frog, they put it into a bucket.

37
00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:04.397
"Are the frogs okay?"

38
00:02:04.717 --> 00:02:07.679
Cole called, rushing over and looking into the buckets.

39
00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:09.881
"Do any of them look sick?"

40
00:02:11.061 --> 00:02:12.823
A girl named Daisy looked at him.

41
00:02:13.883 --> 00:02:16.545
She was two years ahead of Henry and Cole in school.

42
00:02:16.565 --> 00:02:20.528
"I think we got them out fast enough," she said.

43
00:02:22.069 --> 00:02:24.991
An older kid named John gave Cole a dirty look.

44
00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:28.713
"Yeah. No thanks to you, frog boy!"

45
00:02:29.094 --> 00:02:29.594
he said.

46
00:02:30.615 --> 00:02:32.216
Coach Phillips stepped forward.

47
00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:36.361
He was a cheerful man, who was almost always smiling.

48
00:02:37.462 --> 00:02:39.803
But Henry could see that he wasn't smiling now.

49
00:02:39.823 --> 00:02:44.024
"That's enough," the swim coach told John.

50
00:02:44.044 --> 00:02:47.686
"Everyone is innocent until proven guilty."

51
00:02:48.706 --> 00:02:49.867
"Okay, Coach."

52
00:02:51.067 --> 00:02:51.848
John shrugged.

53
00:02:51.868 --> 00:02:55.829
"But everyone knows who the frog lover is around here."

54
00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:58.330
A couple of kids nodded.

55
00:02:59.431 --> 00:03:02.332
Others stared at Cole suspiciously or looked confused.

56
00:03:04.068 --> 00:03:06.250
"Uh-oh," Henry whispered to Maggie.

57
00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:08.372
"Cole was right.

58
00:03:09.473 --> 00:03:10.814
He's the main suspect!

59
00:03:11.795 --> 00:03:13.356
We'd better start investigating!"

60
00:03:14.497 --> 00:03:17.740
"How are we supposed to figure out who put the frogs in the pool?"

61
00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:18.861
Maggie asked.

62
00:03:18.881 --> 00:03:22.043
"We can't check the frogs for fingerprints!"

63
00:03:22.063 --> 00:03:25.446
"Good point," Henry said with a grin.

64
00:03:25.466 --> 00:03:29.109
"But we can split up and start talking to people.

65
00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:32.132
Maybe someone saw what really happened."

66
00:03:33.588 --> 00:03:34.889
"Okay," Maggie said.

67
00:03:34.909 --> 00:03:37.151
"I'll go question Daisy."

68
00:03:38.231 --> 00:03:38.992
She walked away.

69
00:03:41.033 --> 00:03:41.974
Henry looked around.

70
00:03:43.055 --> 00:03:46.677
Belltown was pretty small, so he knew almost everyone at the pool.

71
00:03:47.818 --> 00:03:50.900
A kid who lived across the street from him was standing in the water.

72
00:03:52.341 --> 00:03:54.983
His name was Arnold, but everyone called him Tiny.

73
00:03:55.964 --> 00:03:59.846
The nickname was a joke because Tiny was the tallest kid in the tenth grade.

74
00:03:59.866 --> 00:04:03.781
"Hi, Tiny," Henry said, walking over.

75
00:04:03.801 --> 00:04:06.682
"Hi, Henry," Tiny said.

76
00:04:06.702 --> 00:04:10.023
"Did you come to help us catch these frogs?"

77
00:04:11.264 --> 00:04:12.164
Henry smiled.

78
00:04:13.425 --> 00:04:16.086
"Sorry, I just came to watch the tryouts.

79
00:04:17.427 --> 00:04:19.287
So I don't have my swimsuit on."

80
00:04:19.307 --> 00:04:21.648
"That's okay."

81
00:04:22.749 --> 00:04:24.129
Tiny looked around the pool.

82
00:04:24.149 --> 00:04:27.231
"I think we got most of them already."

83
00:04:28.411 --> 00:04:29.592
Henry looked around too.

84
00:04:30.712 --> 00:04:32.813
He saw two frogs still swimming around.

85
00:04:33.933 --> 00:04:35.533
The rest were already in the buckets.

86
00:04:35.553 --> 00:04:38.914
"Is everyone here trying out for the team?"

87
00:04:39.214 --> 00:04:40.115
he asked Tiny.

88
00:04:40.135 --> 00:04:42.615
"Not exactly."

89
00:04:42.975 --> 00:04:43.756
Tiny shrugged.

90
00:04:43.776 --> 00:04:49.697
"There are only six spots on the team, and five of them are already taken.

91
00:04:50.817 --> 00:04:53.658
I've been on the team all summer, so I have one of the spots.

92
00:04:54.859 --> 00:04:59.740
The Farley twins, Mary Martinez, and John Miller are already on the team too."

93
00:05:00.864 --> 00:05:03.446
Just then Henry saw a frog swim past.

94
00:05:05.727 --> 00:05:06.327
"There's one!"

95
00:05:06.627 --> 00:05:07.128
he cried.

96
00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:10.169
Tiny swam after the frog.

97
00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:14.292
He chased it halfway to the other end and finally caught it.

98
00:05:15.532 --> 00:05:17.093
Henry carried a bucket closer.

99
00:05:18.194 --> 00:05:19.494
Tiny swam over to him.

100
00:05:19.514 --> 00:05:23.677
"How many people are trying out for the last spot on the team?"

101
00:05:24.037 --> 00:05:26.498
Henry asked as Tiny put the frog in the bucket.

102
00:05:26.518 --> 00:05:29.320
"Four," Tiny said.

103
00:05:30.432 --> 00:05:33.013
"Your friend Cole and three other people."

104
00:05:33.033 --> 00:05:35.574
"Wow," Henry said.

105
00:05:35.594 --> 00:05:39.155
"Four swimmers trying out for one spot.

106
00:05:40.135 --> 00:05:41.495
That's a lot of competition."

107
00:05:41.515 --> 00:05:46.817
"If you ask me, Cole is the best swimmer of the four," Tiny said.

108
00:05:46.837 --> 00:05:49.458
"He'll probably get the spot."

109
00:05:50.818 --> 00:05:53.059
Just then a young girl walked past.

110
00:05:54.279 --> 00:05:56.920
She was one of the few kids that Henry didn't recognize.

111
00:05:58.224 --> 00:06:00.689
She stopped when she heard what Tiny had just said.

112
00:06:00.709 --> 00:06:02.853
"Don't be so sure!"

113
00:06:03.153 --> 00:06:04.776
the girl said, glaring at Tiny.

114
00:06:04.796 --> 00:06:10.406
"Cole definitely won't be getting a spot on the team if I have anything to say about it!"
